# Untracked, gitignored files that Claude Code copies into a worktree it
# creates (`claude --worktree <name>`). It copies rather than symlinks, and it
# only ever considers files that are both untracked and ignored, so nothing
# tracked can be affected from here.
#
# Deliberately just `.env`, and it should stay small:
#
#   - `node_modules` is expanded and copied file by file by this mechanism,
#     which is the wrong tool for 622 packages. scripts/wt-bootstrap.sh clones
#     it in one operation instead.
#   - `.next` and `nucarpool-db-data/` are generated per checkout; a copy would
#     be stale at best and, for the database directory, a second MySQL data
#     directory nobody asked for.
#   - `.env.production` is written by the Amplify build container from real
#     deployment credentials. It must never exist on a developer machine, let
#     alone be propagated into a worktree.
#
# This runs only when the worktree is first created, not when one is resumed.
.env
